.TH SDL_CreatePalette 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreatePalette \- Create a palette structure with the specified number of color entries.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_pixels.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Palette * SDL_CreatePalette(int ncolors);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If
.BR ncolors
is larger than the palette\(aqs size -
.BR firstcolor ,
it is truncated to the amount that will fit\[char46]
.PP
The palette entries are initialized to white\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I ncolors
represents the number of color entries in the color palette\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a new
.BR SDL_Palette
structure on success or NULL on failure (e\[char46]g\[char46] if there wasn\(aqt enough memory); call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

